    readme: "# \ud83d\ude80 Featured Software Projects & Applied AI Showcase\n\n[![Author: Sagnik Nag](https://img.shields.io/badge/Author-Sagnik%20Nag-0A66C2?style=for-the-badge&logo=linkedin&logoColor=white)](https://github.com/sagnikkhaze-lgtm)\n[![Focus: Applied AI & Software Engineering](https://img.shields.io/badge/Focus-Applied%20AI%20%26%20Software%20Engineering-FF6F00?style=for-the-badge)](https://github.com/sagnikkhaze-lgtm)\n[![Language: Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.10+-3776AB?style=for-the-badge&logo=python&logoColor=white)](https://www.python.org/)\n[![Framework: LangChain](https://img.shields.io/badge/Framework-LangChain-1C3C3C?style=for-the-badge&logo=langchain&logoColor=white)](https://www.langchain.com/)\n[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg?style=for-the-badge)](LICENSE)\n\nA curated portfolio of **flagship software applications**, **applied GenAI mini-products**, and **developer tools**. Each project in this repository is built end-to-end with modular architecture, strict security best practices, and detailed documentation.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcd1 Table of Contents\n\n- [Featured Projects Showcase](#-featured-projects-showcase)\n- [Project Deep Dives](#-project-deep-dives)\n  - [1. \ud83d\udca1 Tech Jargon Explainer (GenAI Web App)](#1--tech-jargon-explainer-genai-web-app)\n- [Repository Structure](#-repository-structure)\n- [Engineering Standards](#-engineering-standards)\n- [Author & Contact](#-author--contact)\n- [License](#-license)\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udf1f Featured Projects Showcase\n\n| # | Project | Domain / Stack | Key Highlights | Link |\n| :-: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :-: |\n| **01** | **Tech Jargon Explainer** | `Python` `LangChain` `OpenAI GPT-4o` `Gradio` | Interactive LLM web application translating intricate tech concepts into plain English with real-world analogies under 30 words. | [View Project](01-tech-jargon-explainer/) |\n\n*(More flagship projects added regularly as they reach production quality)*\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd0d Project Deep Dives\n\n### 1. \ud83d\udca1 Tech Jargon Explainer (GenAI Web App)\n> *Directory: [`01-tech-jargon-explainer/`](01-tech-jargon-explainer/)*\n\n- **Problem**: Technical jargon (*Docker, Webhooks, Vector DBs, Latency*) acts as a communication barrier between engineers and non-technical stakeholders.\n- **Solution**: An AI-powered explainer web app that employs targeted few-shot prompt engineering with OpenAI's `gpt-4o-mini` to deliver concise, analogy-driven explanations.\n- **Tech Stack**:\n  - **LLM Orchestration**: LangChain (`init_chat_model`, `PromptTemplate`)\n  - **Model**: OpenAI `gpt-4o-mini`\n  - **UI / Frontend**: Gradio Web Interface\n  - **Environment & Security**: `python-dotenv` for encrypted credential handling\n\n#### Architecture:\n```\nUser Query (e.g. \"Kubernetes\")\n       \u2502\n       \u25bc\nLangChain PromptTemplate (Guiding: Plain English + <30 Words + Analogy)\n       \u2502\n       \u25bc\nOpenAI GPT-4o-mini (Low-latency inference)\n       \u2502\n       \u25bc\nGradio Web Interface (Real-time reactive output)\n```\n\n#### Quick Start:\n```bash\ncd 01-tech-jargon-explainer\npip install -r requirements.txt\ncp .env.example .env   # Add your OPENAI_API_KEY\npython3 llm.py\n```\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcc2 Repository Structure\n\n```\nfeatured-software-projects/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md                          <-- Master Portfolio & Showcase Index\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 LICENSE                            <-- MIT Open-Source License\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 .gitignore                         <-- Comprehensive security & environment ignores\n\u2502\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 01-tech-jargon-explainer/          <-- Project 01: LangChain + Gradio AI App\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 llm.py                         <-- Application logic & UI runner\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 requirements.txt               <-- Locked dependencies\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 .env.example                   <-- Template for required environment keys\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 README.md                      <-- Project-specific technical documentation\n\u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 (Future Featured Projects)\n```\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Engineering & Security Standards\n\n- \ud83d\udd12 **Zero-Leak Policy**: All sensitive keys (`.env`) are strictly excluded via `.gitignore` and provided via `.env.example` templates.\n- \ud83d\udce6 **Reproducible Builds**: Every project includes independent dependency manifests (`requirements.txt` / `package.json`).\n- \ud83d\udcd6 **Complete Documentation**: Every subproject contains an isolated README detailing architectural choices, dependencies, and execution recipes.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udc64 Author & Contact\n\n**Sagnik Nag**\n- **GitHub**: [@sagnikkhaze-lgtm](https://github.com/sagnikkhaze-lgtm)\n- **Institution**: *St. Xavier's College, Kolkata*\n- **Email**: `sagnikk.haze@gmail.com`\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcc4 License\n\nThis repository is licensed under the [MIT License](LICENSE).\n",
